{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Gopher.</b> It is the name of a light wood that floats on water, and it has no parallel in Scripture." "<b>Rooms.</b> Because every animal, bird, and beast, man and wife — they are male and female alone." "And it is called 'tevah' and not 'sefinah,' because it is not in the shape of a ship and has no oars." "<b>And you shall pitch it.</b> Some say it is from the root כפרת, and the meaning is a covering of pitch. Some say that the kopher is like pitch. Some say there is clay in the earth from the dust, and it adheres and hardens like pitch. Some say it is what is called in the language of Ishmael with substitution of qof for kaf. The correct view is that the word 'וכפרת' is from the root בכופר." "<b>From within.</b> Like 'inside.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {3 "The text is elliptical throughout; each 'some say' lacks an explicit object. The third and fourth opinions omit the actual Arabic word Ibn Ezra alludes to. Translated hyper-literally without supplying the missing terms."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:32.837155911Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}